From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:35:59 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/37] Share the window's scene and the device host with
 Iris's UIKit

Iris's UIKit (OpenUIKit in Iris's runtimes/ios) draws into the same render
core scene and runs as the same Device Protocol device, so what both need
moves to the IrisHost target there: the scene with its fonts and version
counter, how irisrun asked the app to run (IRISRUN_DEVICE, IRISRUN_SCALE,
IRISRUN_FRAMES), the device host with its envelopes, frame scheduling and
JPEG encoding, the script commands and the PNG writer. OpenSwiftUI keeps
what is its own: rendering the view graph for each update, and DeviceInput,
which now takes IrisHost's touches.
---
